// Diagnostic codes the BACKEND can emit. The one `*_codes.npk` of Phase B so far.
//
// Cycle 0.7.7. `check_codes_centralised` holds the rule: no code appears as a
// literal at the site that emits it, because a mistyped literal silently invents
// a new code.

mod:emit_codes;

// Construct not supported at this backend rung (SUBSET_1 §3). It must name the
// CONSTRUCT and the RUNG that enables it, so the message is actionable rather
// than a refusal — and it is NEVER a parse error, because the parser never
// restricts (D-085).
pub func:RUNG_UNSUPPORTED = string() never fails { pass "NITPICK-RUNG-001"; };

// The emitter met a node it has no classification for. This is a defect in the
// COMPILER, not in the program: Phase A promised the program is valid, and a
// kind nobody classified is a hole in Phase B's coverage of that promise. A
// distinct code so it can never be mistaken for the program's fault.
pub func:EMIT_INTERNAL = string() never fails { pass "NITPICK-EMIT-002"; };
